{
  "category": "Ember Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "From its beak, it expels embers that set the tall grass on fire. Then it pounces on the bewildered prey that pop out of the grass.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hotter the flame sac on its belly, the faster it can fly, but it takes some time to get the fire going.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "From its beak, it expels embers that set the tall grass on fire. Then it pounces on the bewildered prey that pop out of the grass.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hotter the flame sac on its belly, the faster it can fly, but it takes some time to get the fire going.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "From its beak, it fires embers at its prey. Once it has caught them, it grills them at high heat before feasting upon them.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "It will not tolerate other Fletchinder entering its territory, which has a radius of several miles.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "It scatters embers in the tall grass. Then bug Pokémon, frightened by the flames, come flying out, and Fletchinder gobbles them up.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its speed right after takeoff already puts it in the top speed class of all bird Pokémon.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fletchinder launches embers into the den of its prey. When the prey comes leaping out, Fletchinder’s sharp talons finish it off.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fletchinder are exceedingly territorial and aggressive. These Pokémon fight among themselves over feeding grounds.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
